When over 60% of DEX volume comes from automated systems, a manual trader
who spots a signal and takes 40 seconds to act is no longer trading in the same market conditions they observed.
By the time they execute, bots have already reacted, prices have adjusted, 
and the opportunity window has shifted — meaning their perceived window (what they see on X)
and their actual execution window (when their tx lands) are fundamentally disconnected.
